  ('tear them to pieces', 'tear them to pieces', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"tear them to pieces","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"把他们撕成碎片","example":{"en":"“Go to those people,” said the Witch, “and tear them to pieces.”","cn":"“去把那些人撕成碎片！”女巫说。"},"note":"指将某物撕裂成小碎片，或喻指严厉批评。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1125]}'::jsonb),
  ('at full speed', 'at full speed', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"at full speed","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"全速地","example":{"en":"“Very well,” said the wolf, and he dashed away at full speed, followed by the others.","cn":"“好嘞！”狼说，然后它就飞快地冲了出去，其他狼也跟着它。"},"note":"指以最快的速度。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1129]}'::jsonb),
  ('put down', 'put down', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"put down","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"放下","example":{"en":"Then he put down his axe and sat beside the Scarecrow, who said, “It was a good fight, friend.”","cn":"然后他放下斧子，坐在稻草人旁边，稻草人说：“朋友，你打得真棒！”"},"note":"表示将某物放下。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1135]}'::jsonb),
  ('made up her mind', 'made up her mind', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"made up her mind","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"下定决心","example":{"en":"She could not understand how all her plans to destroy these strangers had failed; but she was a powerful Witch, as well as a wicked one, and she soon made up her mind how to act.","cn":"她不明白，为什么她想赶走这些陌生人的办法都失败了。不过她是个很厉害、也很坏的女巫，所以她很快就想好了下一步该怎么做。"},"note":"指决定做某事。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1172]}'::jsonb),
  ('driven him out of', 'driven him out of', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"driven him out of","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"把他赶出了","example":{"en":"The second time was when she had fought against the Great Oz himself, and driven him out of the land of the West.","cn":"第二次是她和厉害的奥兹大王打架，把他赶出了西边的土地。"},"note":"指将某人或某物从某地赶走。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1180]}'::jsonb),
  ('scared away', 'scared away', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"scared away","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"吓走了","example":{"en":"But now that her fierce wolves and her wild crows and her stinging bees were gone, and her slaves had been scared away by the Cowardly Lion, she saw there was only one way left to destroy Dorothy and her friends.","cn":"可是现在，她的坏狼、野乌鸦和会蜇人的蜜蜂都跑光了。她的奴隶也被胆小的狮子吓走了。她发现，只剩下最后一个办法可以赶走多萝西和她的朋友们了。"},"note":"指将某人或某物吓跑。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1183]}'::jsonb),
  ('stumbled over', 'stumbled over', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"stumbled over","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"绊倒在","example":{"en":"So that when Dorothy walked across the floor she stumbled over the bar, not being able to see it, and fell at full length.","cn":"这样当多萝西走过地板时，她会绊倒在铁棍上，因为她看不见它，然后就摔了个大跟头。"},"note":"指被…绊倒。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1252]}'::jsonb),
  ('snatched it away', 'snatched it away', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"snatched it away","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"一把抢走了","example":{"en":"She was not much hurt, but in her fall one of the Silver Shoes came off; and before she could reach it, the Witch had snatched it away and put it on her own skinny foot.","cn":"她没有受太大的伤，但是她摔倒的时候，一只银鞋掉了下来；还没等她捡起来，女巫就一把抢走了，穿在了自己瘦瘦的脚上。"},"note":"指迅速抢走某物。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1253]}'::jsonb),
  ('put it on', 'put it on', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"put it on","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"穿在了","example":{"en":"She was not much hurt, but in her fall one of the Silver Shoes came off; and before she could reach it, the Witch had snatched it away and put it on her own skinny foot.","cn":"她没有受太大的伤，但是她摔倒的时候，一只银鞋掉了下来；还没等她捡起来，女巫就一把抢走了，穿在了自己瘦瘦的脚上。"},"note":"表示穿戴上某物。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1253]}'::jsonb),
  ('from head to foot', 'from head to foot', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"from head to foot","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"从头到脚","example":{"en":"This made Dorothy so very angry that she picked up the bucket of water that stood near and dashed it over the Witch, wetting her from head to foot.","cn":"这让多萝西非常生气，以至于她拿起旁边的一桶水，朝女巫泼过去，把她从头到脚都弄湿了。"},"note":"形容全身。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1259]}'::jsonb),
  ('melt away', 'melt away', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"melt away","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"融化","example":{"en":"“See what you have done!” she screamed. “In a minute I shall melt away.”","cn":"“看你做了什么！”她大叫。“我很快就要融化了。”"},"note":"指逐渐融化或消失。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1261]}'::jsonb),
  ('get hold of', 'get hold of', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"get hold of","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"得到/抓住","example":{"en":"Her bees and her crows and her wolves were lying in heaps and drying up, and she had used up all the power of the Golden Cap; but if she could only get hold of the Silver Shoes, they would give her more power than all the other things she had lost.","cn":"她的蜜蜂、乌鸦和狼都堆成一堆，枯萎了，她也用光了金冠所有的魔力；但是如果她能得到银鞋，它们会给她比她失去的所有东西加起来还要多的力量。"},"note":"指获得或抓住某物。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1245]}'::jsonb),
  ('set him free', 'set him free', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"set him free","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"释放他","example":{"en":"The Cowardly Lion was much pleased to hear that the Wicked Witch had been melted by a bucket of water, and Dorothy at once unlocked the gate of his prison and set him free.","cn":"胆小的狮子听说坏女巫被一桶水融化了，非常开心。多萝西立刻打开了牢房的门，放他出来了。"},"note":"意为使某人获得自由。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1274]}'::jsonb),
  ('made to work hard', 'made to work hard', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"made to work hard","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"被迫辛苦工作","example":{"en":"There was great rejoicing among the yellow Winkies, for they had been made to work hard during many years for the Wicked Witch, who had always treated them with great cruelty.","cn":"黄色的温基人们都非常高兴，因为他们被坏女巫逼着辛苦工作了很多年。坏女巫总是对他们很坏。"},"note":"表示某人被迫做某事。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1276]}'::jsonb),
  ('spent the time in feasting and dancing', 'spent the time in feasting and dancing', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"spent the time in feasting and dancing","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"花时间吃喝玩乐","example":{"en":"They kept this day as a holiday, then and ever after, and spent the time in feasting and dancing.","cn":"从那天起，他们就把这一天当作节日，一直庆祝下去，唱歌跳舞，开心地吃喝玩乐。"},"note":"意为将时间用于某活动。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1277]}'::jsonb),
  ('a number of', 'a number of', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"a number of","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"许多，一些","example":{"en":"So she chose a number of the Winkies who looked as if they knew the most, and they all started away.","cn":"于是她选了一些看起来最聪明的温基人，他们就出发了。"},"note":"表示一些或若干。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1282]}'::jsonb),
  ('broken off', 'broken off', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"broken off","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"折断了","example":{"en":"His axe was near him, but the blade was rusted and the handle broken off short.","cn":"他的斧头就在旁边，可是斧刃生锈了，斧柄也断成了两截。"},"note":"意为某物被从主体上折断。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1284]}'::jsonb),
  ('shedding a few tears', 'shedding a few tears', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"shedding a few tears","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"流了几滴眼泪","example":{"en":"The Winkies lifted him tenderly in their arms, and carried him back to the Yellow Castle again, Dorothy shedding a few tears by the way at the sad plight of her old friend, and the Lion looking sober and sorry.","cn":"温基人们轻轻地把他抱起来，又把他带回了黄色的城堡。一路上，多萝西看到老朋友这么可怜，流了几滴眼泪。狮子看着也很严肃，很难过。"},"note":"意为哭泣。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1285]}'::jsonb),
  ('straighten out', 'straighten out', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"straighten out","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"弄直，解决","example":{"en":"And when the tinsmiths came, bringing with them all their tools in baskets, she inquired, “Can you straighten out those dents in the Tin Woodman, and bend him back into shape again, and solder him together where he is broken?”","cn":"铁匠们提着工具筐来了。她问：“你们能把铁皮人身上的坑弄平，让他变回原来的样子，再把断掉的地方焊起来吗？”"},"note":"意为使某物变直或解决问题。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1291]}'::jsonb),
  ('as good as ever', 'as good as ever', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"as good as ever","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"和以前一样好","example":{"en":"The tinsmiths looked the Woodman over carefully and then answered that they thought they could mend him so he would be as good as ever.","cn":"铁匠们仔细看了看铁皮人，然后说他们能把他修好，让他和以前一样。"},"note":"表示和以往一样优秀或良好。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1292]}'::jsonb),
  ('did a good job', 'did a good job', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"did a good job","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"干得好","example":{"en":"To be sure, there were several patches on him, but the tinsmiths did a good job, and as the Woodman was not a vain man he did not mind the patches at all.","cn":"当然，他身上多了几块补丁，但铁匠们手艺很好。而且铁皮人一点也不臭美，所以他一点也不介意这些补丁。"},"note":"意为把工作做得很好。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1294]}'::jsonb),
  ('wept tears of joy', 'wept tears of joy', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"wept tears of joy","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"喜极而泣","example":{"en":"When, at last, he walked into Dorothy’s room and thanked her for rescuing him, he was so pleased that he wept tears of joy, and Dorothy had to wipe every tear carefully from his face with her apron, so his joints would not be rusted.","cn":"他终于走进多萝西的房间，感谢她救了他。他高兴得流下了眼泪，多萝西赶紧用围裙擦掉他脸上的每一滴泪水，免得他的关节生锈。"},"note":"意为因高兴而流泪。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1295]}'::jsonb),
  ('at the same time', 'at the same time', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"at the same time","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"同时","example":{"en":"At the same time her own tears fell thick and fast at the joy of meeting her old friend again, and these tears did not need to be wiped away.","cn":"同时，她也因为又见到老朋友而高兴得哗哗地流下了眼泪，这些眼泪倒不用擦掉。"},"note":"表示在同一时间发生。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1296]}'::jsonb),
  ('was obliged to go out', 'was obliged to go out', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"was obliged to go out","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"不得不出去","example":{"en":"As for the Lion, he wiped his eyes so often with the tip of his tail that it became quite wet, and he was obliged to go out into the courtyard and hold it in the sun till it dried.","cn":"而狮子呢，他用尾巴尖擦眼睛擦得太频繁了，结果尾巴尖都湿透了。他只好跑到院子里，把尾巴放在太阳下晒干。"},"note":"意为被迫或有责任做某事。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1297]}'::jsonb),
  ('chop it down', 'chop it down', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"chop it down","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"砍倒它","example":{"en":"It was a very tall tree, and the trunk was so smooth that no one could climb it; but the Woodman said at once, “I’ll chop it down, and then we can get the Scarecrow’s clothes.”","cn":"那是一棵很高很高的树，树干太光滑了，没有人能爬上去。但铁皮人马上说：“我把它砍倒，这样我们就能拿到稻草人的衣服了。”"},"note":"意为砍伐使树木倒下。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1301]}'::jsonb),
  ('instead of', 'instead of', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"instead of","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"代替，而不是","example":{"en":"Now while the tinsmiths had been at work mending the Woodman himself, another of the Winkies, who was a goldsmith, had made an axe-handle of solid gold and fitted it to the Woodman’s axe, instead of the old broken handle.","cn":"就在铁匠们修理铁皮人的时候，另一个温基人（他是个金匠）用纯金给铁皮人做了一个新斧柄，替换掉了旧的坏掉的斧柄。"},"note":"表示替代或作为…的替代品。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1302]}'::jsonb),
  ('as soon as he had spoken', 'as soon as he had spoken', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"as soon as he had spoken","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"他刚说完就","example":{"en":"As soon as he had spoken, the Tin Woodman began to chop, and in a short time the tree fell over with a crash, whereupon the Scarecrow’s clothes fell out of the branches and rolled off on the ground.","cn":"他刚说完，铁皮人就开始砍树了。没多久，大树就轰隆一声倒了下来，稻草人的衣服也从树枝上掉了下来，滚到地上。"},"note":"表示一件事情紧接着另一件事情发生。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1304]}'::jsonb),
  ('in a short time', 'in a short time', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"in a short time","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"很快，不一会儿","example":{"en":"As soon as he had spoken, the Tin Woodman began to chop, and in a short time the tree fell over with a crash, whereupon the Scarecrow’s clothes fell out of the branches and rolled off on the ground.","cn":"他刚说完，铁皮人就开始砍树了。没多久，大树就轰隆一声倒了下来，稻草人的衣服也从树枝上掉了下来，滚到地上。"},"note":"表示在短时间内。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1304]}'::jsonb),
  ('picked them up', 'picked them up', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"picked them up","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"捡起它们","example":{"en":"Dorothy picked them up and had the Winkies carry them back to the castle, where they were stuffed with nice, clean straw; and behold! here was the Scarecrow, as good as ever, thanking them over and over again for saving him.","cn":"多萝西把衣服捡起来，让温基人背回城堡。在那里，人们把衣服里塞满了干净的稻草。瞧！稻草人又变回了原来的样子，不停地感谢他们救了他。"},"note":"意为拿起地上的东西。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1305]}'::jsonb),
  ('over and over again', 'over and over again', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"over and over again","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"反复地，一再地","example":{"en":"Dorothy picked them up and had the Winkies carry them back to the castle, where they were stuffed with nice, clean straw; and behold! here was the Scarecrow, as good as ever, thanking them over and over again for saving him.","cn":"多萝西把衣服捡起来，让温基人背回城堡。在那里，人们把衣服里塞满了干净的稻草。瞧！稻草人又变回了原来的样子，不停地感谢他们救了他。"},"note":"表示重复多次。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1305]}'::jsonb),
  ('now that they were reunited', 'now that they were reunited', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"now that they were reunited","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"既然他们重聚了","example":{"en":"Now that they were reunited, Dorothy and her friends spent a few happy days at the Yellow Castle, where they found everything they needed to make them comfortable.","cn":"大家又聚到一起了，多萝西和她的朋友们在黄城堡里度过了几天开心的日子。在那里，他们想要什么就有什么，过得很舒服。"},"note":"表示由于某种原因或条件。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1306]}'::jsonb),
  ('claim his promise', 'claim his promise', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"claim his promise","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"要求他兑现承诺","example":{"en":"But one day the girl thought of Aunt Em, and said, “We must go back to Oz, and claim his promise.”","cn":"但有一天，女孩想起了艾姆婶婶，说：“我们得回到奥兹大王那里，让他兑现承诺了。”"},"note":"意为要求履行诺言。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1307]}'::jsonb),
  ('not even', 'not even', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"not even","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"甚至没有；连...都没有。","example":{"en":"You will remember there was no road—not even a pathway—between the castle of the Wicked Witch and the Emerald City.","cn":"你还记得吗？从坏女巫的城堡到翡翠城，根本没有路，连小道都没有。"},"note":"用于强调否定，表示程度更深。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1322]}'::jsonb),
  ('in search of', 'in search of', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"in search of","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"寻找；寻求。","example":{"en":"When the four travelers went in search of the Witch she had seen them coming, and so sent the Winged Monkeys to bring them to her.","cn":"四个旅行者去找巫婆时，巫婆看到了他们。于是她派飞猴把他们带到她那儿。"},"note":"固定短语，表示去寻找某物或某人而努力。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1323]}'::jsonb),
  ('find their way back', 'find their way back', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"find their way back","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"找到回去的路。","example":{"en":"It was much harder to find their way back through the big fields of buttercups and yellow daisies than it was being carried.","cn":"穿过一大片毛茛花和黄色雏菊地，要自己找路回去，比被带着走难多了。"},"note":"常用于描述在迷路后找到返回路线。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1324]}'::jsonb),
  ('started off', 'started off', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"started off","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"出发；开始。","example":{"en":"They knew, of course, they must go straight east, toward the rising sun; and they started off in the right way.","cn":"他们知道，他们必须一直往东走，朝着太阳升起的方向。他们一开始走得很对。"},"note":"短语动词，常指开始一段旅程或一个活动。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1325]}'::jsonb),
  ('were lost in', 'were lost in', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"were lost in","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"迷失在...中。","example":{"en":"But at noon, when the sun was over their heads, they did not know which was east and which was west, and that was the reason they were lost in the great fields.","cn":"但到了中午，太阳在他们头顶时，他们就分不清哪里是东哪里是西了。所以他们迷失在了大片田地里。"},"note":"表示在某个地方找不到方向。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1326]}'::jsonb),
  ('kept on walking', 'kept on walking', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"kept on walking","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"继续走路。","example":{"en":"They kept on walking, however, and at night the moon came out and shone brightly.","cn":"不过他们继续往前走。到了晚上，月亮出来了，亮亮地照着。"},"note":"\"keep on doing sth\" 意为“继续做某事”，强调动作的持续。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1327]}'::jsonb),
  ('at night', 'at night', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"at night","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"在晚上。","example":{"en":"They kept on walking, however, and at night the moon came out and shone brightly.","cn":"不过他们继续往前走。到了晚上，月亮出来了，亮亮地照着。"},"note":"常用于指夜间。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1327]}'::jsonb),
  ('came out', 'came out', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"came out","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"出来；出现。","example":{"en":"They kept on walking, however, and at night the moon came out and shone brightly.","cn":"不过他们继续往前走。到了晚上，月亮出来了，亮亮地照着。"},"note":"短语动词，表示从内部到外部，或某个事物显现。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1327]}'::jsonb),
  ('all but', 'all but', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"all but","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"除了...都。","example":{"en":"So they lay down among the sweet smelling yellow flowers and slept soundly until morning—all but the Scarecrow and the Tin Woodman.","cn":"于是他们躺在香香的黄花中间，睡得很香，直到天亮——除了稻草人和铁皮人。"},"note":"相当于 \"all except\"，表示排除某种情况或某人。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1328]}'::jsonb),
  ('come to', 'come to', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"come to","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"到达；来到。","example":{"en":"“If we walk far enough,” said Dorothy, “I am sure we shall sometime come to some place.”","cn":"多萝西说：“如果我们走得够远，我肯定我们总会走到某个地方的。”"},"note":"短语动词，指抵达某个目的地。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1330]}'::jsonb),
  ('day by day', 'day by day', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"day by day","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"日复一日地。","example":{"en":"But day by day passed away, and they still saw nothing before them but the scarlet fields.","cn":"但一天天过去了，他们眼前除了那红色的田野，什么也没看到。"},"note":"强调时间一天天过去，常用于描述持续变化。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1331]}'::jsonb),
