  ('went back to', 'went back to', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"went back to","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"回到","example":{"en":"Almost as quickly as it came the head went back to the body, and the man laughed harshly as he said, “It isn’t as easy as you think!”","cn":"他的头几乎一下子就缩了回去，那个人大声地笑着说：“这可不像你想的那么容易！”"},"note":"指返回到某个地方或状态。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1986]}'::jsonb),
  ('up the hill', 'up the hill', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"up the hill","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"上山","example":{"en":"The Lion became quite angry at the laughter caused by the Scarecrow’s mishap, and giving a loud roar that echoed like thunder, he dashed up the hill.","cn":"狮子看到稻草人摔倒了，大家还在笑，他很生气。他大吼一声，声音像打雷一样响，然后冲上了山。"},"note":"表示沿着山坡向上移动。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1988]}'::jsonb),
  ('to his feet', 'to his feet', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"to his feet","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"站起来","example":{"en":"Dorothy ran down and helped the Scarecrow to his feet, and the Lion came up to her, feeling rather bruised and sore, and said, “It is useless to fight people with shooting heads; no one can withstand them.”","cn":"多萝西跑下去扶起稻草人，狮子走到她身边，感觉自己又青又痛，说：“和这些会伸头打人的家伙打架没用，谁也打不过他们。”"},"note":"常用搭配为 \"help someone to their feet\" 或 \"struggle to one''s feet\"。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1990]}'::jsonb),
  ('useless to', 'useless to', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"useless to","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"做...没用","example":{"en":"Dorothy ran down and helped the Scarecrow to his feet, and the Lion came up to her, feeling rather bruised and sore, and said, “It is useless to fight people with shooting heads; no one can withstand them.”","cn":"多萝西跑下去扶起稻草人，狮子走到她身边，感觉自己又青又痛，说：“和这些会伸头打人的家伙打架没用，谁也打不过他们。”"},"note":"常用结构为 \"it is useless to do something\"。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1990]}'::jsonb),
  ('the right to', 'the right to', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"the right to","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"做...的权利","example":{"en":"“You have still the right to command them once more.”","cn":"“你还可以再命令他们一次。”"},"note":"常用结构为 \"have the right to do something\"。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1993]}'::jsonb),
  ('putting on', 'putting on', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"putting on","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"戴上；穿上","example":{"en":"“Very well,” she answered, and putting on the Golden Cap she uttered the magic words.","cn":"“好的。”她回答，然后戴上金冠，念出了神奇的咒语。"},"note":"指穿戴衣物或饰品。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1994]}'::jsonb),
  ('in a few moments', 'in a few moments', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"in a few moments","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"过了一会儿；片刻之后","example":{"en":"The Monkeys were as prompt as ever, and in a few moments the entire band stood before her.","cn":"猴子们像以前一样，很快就来了，不一会儿，所有的猴子都站在了她面前。"},"note":"表示很短的时间。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1995]}'::jsonb),
  ('set them down', 'set them down', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"set them down","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"放下；安放","example":{"en":"As they passed over the hill the Hammer-Heads yelled with vexation, and shot their heads high in the air, but they could not reach the Winged Monkeys, which carried Dorothy and her comrades safely over the hill and set them down in the beautiful country of the Quadlings.","cn":"当他们飞过山的时候，锤头人气得大叫，把头高高地伸向空中，可是他们还是够不着飞猴。飞猴安全地带着多萝西和她的朋友们飞过了山，把他们轻轻地放在了美丽的奎德林人国家。"},"note":"指将某物放置下来。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[1999]}'::jsonb),
  ('in a twinkling', 'in a twinkling', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"in a twinkling","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"一眨眼；瞬间","example":{"en":"“Good-bye, and thank you very much,” returned the girl; and the Monkeys rose into the air and were out of sight in a twinkling.","cn":"“再见，非常谢谢你们！”女孩回答。猴子们飞上了天空，一眨眼就不见了。"},"note":"形容速度非常快。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[2001]}'::jsonb),
  ('field upon field', 'field upon field', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"field upon field","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"一片又一片；连绵不绝的","example":{"en":"There was field upon field of ripening grain, with well-paved roads running between, and pretty rippling brooks with strong bridges across them.","cn":"这里有好多成熟的庄稼地，中间是修得很好的路，还有哗哗流淌的小河，上面架着结实的桥。"},"note":"强调数量很多，范围很大。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[2003]}'::jsonb),
  ('shook the dust out of', 'shook the dust out of', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"shook the dust out of","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"抖掉...上的灰尘","example":{"en":"Before they went to see Glinda, however, they were taken to a room of the Castle, where Dorothy washed her face and combed her hair, and the Lion shook the dust out of his mane, and the Scarecrow patted himself into his best shape, and the Woodman polished his tin and oiled his joints.","cn":"不过，在他们去见格林达之前，他们被带到城堡的一个房间。多萝西洗了脸，梳了头发；狮子抖掉它毛上的灰尘；稻草人把自己拍得美美的；铁皮人擦亮了身体，给关节涂了油。"},"note":"表示通过抖动清除某物上的灰尘。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[2019]}'::jsonb),
  ('looked kindly upon', 'looked kindly upon', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"looked kindly upon","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"亲切地看着","example":{"en":"Her dress was pure white but her eyes were blue, and they looked kindly upon the little girl.","cn":"她的裙子是白色的，但眼睛是蓝色的。她很亲切地看着小姑娘。"},"note":"表示友善、慈爱地看待某人。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[2023]}'::jsonb),
  ('do for you', 'do for you', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"do for you","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"为你做什么","example":{"en":"“What can I do for you, my child?” she asked.","cn":"“孩子，我能帮你什么呢？” 她问。"},"note":"表示能为某人提供什么帮助或服务。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[2024]}'::jsonb),
  ('met with', 'met with', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"met with","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"遇到","example":{"en":"Dorothy told the Witch all her story: how the cyclone had brought her to the Land of Oz, how she had found her companions, and of the wonderful adventures they had met with.","cn":"多萝西把她的故事都告诉了巫师：龙卷风怎么把她带到奥兹国，她怎么找到朋友们，还有他们遇到的那些很棒的冒险。"},"note":"指偶然遇见或经历某事。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[2025]}'::jsonb),
  ('put on mourning', 'put on mourning', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"put on mourning","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"穿丧服/表示哀悼","example":{"en":"“My greatest wish now,” she added, “is to get back to Kansas, for Aunt Em will surely think something dreadful has happened to me, and that will make her put on mourning; and unless the crops are better this year than they were last, I am sure Uncle Henry cannot afford it.”","cn":"“我现在最想的，”她又说，“就是回到堪萨斯身边。因为艾姆婶婶一定会觉得我出了什么可怕的事，她会很难过的。如果今年收成不比去年好，我想亨利叔叔肯定也没钱。”"},"note":"指因悲伤或失去亲人而穿上黑色衣服以示哀悼。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[2026]}'::jsonb),
  ('cannot afford it', 'cannot afford it', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"cannot afford it","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"负担不起","example":{"en":"“My greatest wish now,” she added, “is to get back to Kansas, for Aunt Em will surely think something dreadful has happened to me, and that will make her put on mourning; and unless the crops are better this year than they were last, I am sure Uncle Henry cannot afford it.”","cn":"“我现在最想的，”她又说，“就是回到堪萨斯身边。因为艾姆婶婶一定会觉得我出了什么可怕的事，她会很难过的。如果今年收成不比去年好，我想亨利叔叔肯定也没钱。”"},"note":"表示没有足够的金钱或能力来支付某物或承担某事。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[2026]}'::jsonb),
  ('of no use to', 'of no use to', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"of no use to","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"对...没有用处","example":{"en":"“Willingly!” exclaimed Dorothy; “indeed, it is of no use to me now, and when you have it you can command the Winged Monkeys three times.”","cn":"“没问题！”多萝西大声说，“它现在对我没什么用了。你有了它，就可以让飞猴帮你三次。”"},"note":"表示某物对某人或某事没有价值或用途。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[2030]}'::jsonb),
  ('would be a shame', 'would be a shame', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"would be a shame","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"将会是遗憾的/可惜的","example":{"en":"“By means of the Golden Cap I shall command the Winged Monkeys to carry you to the gates of the Emerald City,” said Glinda, “for it would be a shame to deprive the people of so wonderful a ruler.”","cn":"“我会用金冠让飞猴把你送到翡翠城的城门，”格林达说，“因为让大家失去你这样棒的王，太可惜了。”"},"note":"表示某事令人惋惜或可惜。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[2035]}'::jsonb),
  ('deprive the people of', 'deprive the people of', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"deprive the people of","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"剥夺人们的...","example":{"en":"“By means of the Golden Cap I shall command the Winged Monkeys to carry you to the gates of the Emerald City,” said Glinda, “for it would be a shame to deprive the people of so wonderful a ruler.”","cn":"“我会用金冠让飞猴把你送到翡翠城的城门，”格林达说，“因为让大家失去你这样棒的王，太可惜了。”"},"note":"表示使某人失去某物或某种权利。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[2035]}'::jsonb),
  ('become of you', 'become of you', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"become of you","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"你会怎么样","example":{"en":"Turning to the Tin Woodman, she asked, “What will become of you when Dorothy leaves this country?”","cn":"她转头对铁皮人说，“当多萝西离开这里的时候，你准备做什么？”"},"note":"询问某人的命运或结局。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[2038]}'::jsonb),
  ('rule over', 'rule over', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"rule over","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"统治","example":{"en":"Then he said, “The Winkies were very kind to me, and wanted me to rule over them after the Wicked Witch died.","cn":"然后他说，“温基人对我很好，他们希望我在坏女巫去世后，去当他们的王。”"},"note":"表示对某个地方或人群进行统治。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[2040]}'::jsonb),
  ('like nothing better than', 'like nothing better than', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"like nothing better than","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"最想做的事莫过于","example":{"en":"I am fond of the Winkies, and if I could get back again to the Country of the West, I should like nothing better than to rule over them forever.”","cn":"我喜欢那些温基人。如果我能回到西方国度，我最想做的就是永远统治它们。"},"note":"表示某人最喜欢或最希望做某事。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[2041]}'::jsonb),
  ('used up', 'used up', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"used up","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"用尽","example":{"en":"Then, having used up the powers of the Golden Cap, I shall give it to the King of the Monkeys, that he and his band may thereafter be free for evermore.”","cn":"然后，等金冠的力量用完了，我就把它送给猴子国王，这样他和他的猴子们就可以永远自由了。”"},"note":"表示将某物完全消耗殆尽。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[2048]}'::jsonb),
  ('for evermore', 'for evermore', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"for evermore","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"永远","example":{"en":"Then, having used up the powers of the Golden Cap, I shall give it to the King of the Monkeys, that he and his band may thereafter be free for evermore.”","cn":"然后，等金冠的力量用完了，我就把它送给猴子国王，这样他和他的猴子们就可以永远自由了。”"},"note":"表示永久地，永远地 (较正式)。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[2048]}'::jsonb),
  ('the very first day', 'the very first day', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"the very first day","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"第一天","example":{"en":"“If you had known their power you could have gone back to your Aunt Em the very first day you came to this country.”","cn":"“如果你知道它们有多厉害，你第一天来到这里就能回艾姆婶婶了。”"},"note":"强调是最初的那一天。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[2053]}'::jsonb),
  ('till the end of the world', 'till the end of the world', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"till the end of the world","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"直到世界末日","example":{"en":"“I might have stood and rusted in the forest till the end of the world.”","cn":"“我可能就会在森林里站着，一直生锈，直到世界末日。”"},"note":"表示非常长的时间，直到永远 (夸张)。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[2056]}'::jsonb),
  ('in the wink of an eye', 'in the wink of an eye', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"in the wink of an eye","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"眨眼之间","example":{"en":"And one of the most curious things about them is that they can carry you to any place in the world in three steps, and each step will be made in the wink of an eye.","cn":"它们最特别的一点是，它们可以三步就把你带到世界上的任何地方，每一步都快得像眨眼一样。"},"note":"形容速度非常快，瞬间完成。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[2061]}'::jsonb),
  ('all you have to do', 'all you have to do', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"all you have to do","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"你所要做的就是","example":{"en":"All you have to do is to knock the heels together three times and command the shoes to carry you wherever you wish to go.”","cn":"你只要把鞋跟敲三下，然后命令鞋子带你去你想去的地方就行了。”"},"note":"表示某人唯一需要做的事情。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[2062]}'::jsonb),
  ('threw her arms around', 'threw her arms around', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"threw her arms around","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"抱住","example":{"en":"She threw her arms around the Lion’s neck and kissed him, patting his big head tenderly.","cn":"她抱住狮子的脖子亲了他一下，温柔地拍了拍他的大脑袋。"},"note":"表示用双臂环抱某人。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[2064]}'::jsonb),
  ('at length', 'at length', 'en', 'read-v1', '{"word":"at length","pos":"词块","ipa":"","gloss_cn":"终于","example":{"en":"At length, however, she sat up and looked about her.","cn":"终于，她坐起来，看了看周围。"},"note":"表示经过一段时间后，最终。","kind":"chunk","src_seqs":[2072]}'::jsonb),
